---
layout: base.njk
nav: about
permalink: /about/index.html
title: "About — Inter Sports Infra LLP | Faridabad, India"
description: "Inter Sports Infra LLP is a sports infrastructure contractor based in Faridabad, Haryana, working across India."

hero_eyebrow: "Who we are"
hero_heading: "We Build the<br>Place You <em>Play</em>"
hero_sub: "Inter Sports Infra LLP is a sports infrastructure contractor based in Faridabad, Haryana, working across India. We design and build playing surfaces — and the ground, drainage and civil works beneath them."

story_eyebrow: "Our story"
story_heading: "Built on Years Already on the Ground"
story_paragraphs:
  - "Inter Sports Infra LLP was registered in 2026, but the team behind it has been designing and building sports surfaces for 12+ years. That experience had already delivered 180+ projects — football turf, courts and running tracks — across 24 cities before we came together under this name."
  - "That track record is what the company is built on: knowing which sub-base survives a monsoon, which coat system still holds its pace two summers in, and which detail on a drawing is the one that gets skipped when nobody is checking. We bring that same standard to every client, on one accountable scope from survey to handover."

tiles:
  - value: "12+"
    label: "Years experience"
  - value: "180+"
    label: "Projects delivered"
  - value: "24"
    label: "Cities served"
  - value: "14 L"
    label: "Sq. ft. surfaced"

registered_table:
  caption: "Registered particulars"
  rows:
    - item: "Legal name"
      spec: "Inter Sports Infra LLP"
    - item: "Registered office"
      spec: "Sector 8, Faridabad, Haryana"
    - item: "Scope"
      spec: "Design, civil works, surfacing, AMC"
    - item: "Coverage"
      spec: "Pan-India, four regional bases"

vision_eyebrow: "Our vision"
vision_quote: "Everyone gets the right place, track, and <em>feel to play</em> their favourite sport."
vision_text: "Not the best-funded schools. Not the metros only. Everyone. A child in Ballabhgarh should get a surface that plays as true as one in a private academy — because the specification does not cost more to write correctly."

method_eyebrow: "Our method"
method_heading: "How We Actually Work"
method_intro: "Six stages. You always know which one you are in and what happens next."
method_steps:
  - number: "01"
    title: "Site Visit"
    description: "Levels, orientation, soil, access and where the water currently goes. Free."
  - number: "02"
    title: "Design"
    description: "Layout drawings, build-up section and a written specification."
  - number: "03"
    title: "Quote"
    description: "Fixed scope, itemised. Exclusions printed in the same size as inclusions."
  - number: "04"
    title: "Construction"
    description: "One crew, one supervisor, weekly photographs to your phone."
  - number: "05"
    title: "Handover"
    description: "Joint measurement against the spec, warranty papers, first game played."
  - number: "06"
    title: "Maintenance"
    description: "Annual care so the surface still plays to standard in year five."

materials_eyebrow: "Materials & technology"
materials_heading: "What We Build With"
materials_intro: "We do not manufacture. We specify, and we will name the system on the quote rather than write \"premium imported turf\"."
turf_table:
  caption: "Artificial turf systems"
  rows:
    - item: "Yarn type"
      spec: "Monofilament PE, 8,800–13,000 dtex"
    - item: "Pile height"
      spec: "40 mm hockey / 50–60 mm football"
    - item: "Backing"
      spec: "Woven PP, PU or latex coated"
    - item: "Shock pad"
      spec: "10–15 mm closed-cell PE foam"
    - item: "Infill"
      spec: "Silica sand + SBR / EPDM / TPE"
    - item: "UV stability"
      spec: "8-year yarn warranty typical"
indoor_table:
  caption: "Acrylic, PU & indoor systems"
  rows:
    - item: "Acrylic hard court"
      spec: "6–8 coat system, sand-loaded to pace"
    - item: "PU sports floor"
      spec: "2–4 mm self-levelling polyurethane"
    - item: "EPDM"
      spec: "10–15 mm wet-pour rubber granule"
    - item: "Athletics track"
      spec: "13 mm sandwich or full-PU spray"
    - item: "Indoor vinyl"
      spec: "4.5–7 mm PVC, BWF / FIBA approved"
    - item: "Wooden floor"
      spec: "22 mm maple on sprung batten cradle"
drainage_table:
  caption: "Sub-base & drainage"
  rows:
    - item: "Sub-grade"
      spec: "Compacted to 95% Proctor density"
    - item: "Granular sub-base"
      spec: "150–225 mm graded stone"
    - item: "Binder course"
      spec: "25–40 mm bituminous concrete"
    - item: "Cross fall"
      spec: "1:100 to 1:120, single plane"
    - item: "Perimeter drain"
      spec: "Channel + geotextile-wrapped pipe"
    - item: "Testing"
      spec: "Compaction and flatness recorded"
why_publish_heading: "Why we publish this"
why_publish_paragraphs:
  - "Most sports surface quotes in India name no system, no dtex, no coat count and no compaction figure. That vagueness is where corners get cut after the contract is signed."
  - "Ours names all of it. Take our specification to any other contractor and compare like for like — we would rather win on the number than on the wording."

team_eyebrow: "Who you'll deal with"
team_heading: "A Team That's Done This Before"
team_text: "Every project is handled by our own team of experienced sports infrastructure consultants, project managers and site engineers — not subcontracted labour with no stake in the outcome. The same engineer who writes your specification is the one who inspects the base before the surface goes down, and signs off at handover."

why_eyebrow: "Why choose us"
why_heading: "Five Differences You Can Check"
why_intro: "Every one of these is verifiable before you sign, not a claim about our attitude."
why_cards:
  - number: "01"
    icon_path: "M14 86V14h48l24 24v48zM62 14v24h24M28 56h44"
    title: "Named specifications"
    description: "Dtex, coat count, compaction density and tolerance printed on the quote. Compare us line by line with anyone."
  - number: "02"
    icon_path: "M50 12v76M12 50h76M30 30l40 40M70 30 30 70"
    title: "One accountable scope"
    description: "Civil, surface, marking and equipment under one contract. No vendor pointing at another vendor."
  - number: "03"
    icon_path: "M12 74h76M20 74V44M40 74V28M60 74V38M80 74V20"
    title: "Drainage designed first"
    description: "We set falls and drains before choosing a surface. Most Indian surface failures are water, not material."
  - number: "04"
    icon_path: "M50 10 20 24v28c0 20 13 32 30 38 17-6 30-18 30-38V24z|M38 50l9 9 17-18"
    title: "Written warranty"
    description: "Surface warranty on paper with what is and is not covered, plus an AMC option to keep it valid."
why_checklist:
  - "Weekly site photographs — you see progress without travelling to site."
  - "Honest downgrades — we will tell you when a cheaper surface suits your use."

cta_heading: "Come and See a Finished Site"
cta_text: "We will take you to a project near you so you can walk the surface before you decide anything."
---
<section class="phero">
  <svg class="phero__court" data-draw viewBox="0 0 1440 460" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
    <path d="M70 -40V500" stroke="#2a2e33" stroke-width="3"/>
    <path d="M-40 420H1480" stroke="#2a2e33" stroke-width="3"/>
    <path d="M70 200A220 220 0 0 1 290 420" stroke="#4D8CD4" stroke-width="3"/>
    <path d="M70 60A360 360 0 0 1 430 420" stroke="#1E5B96" stroke-width="2.5"/>
    <path d="M1080 -40V500" stroke="#1c2023" stroke-width="2.5"/>
    <circle cx="1080" cy="190" r="110" stroke="#1c2023" stroke-width="2.5"/>
  </svg>
  <div class="wrap phero__in">
    <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>About</span></nav>
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--on-dark rv">{{ hero_eyebrow }}</p>
    <h1 class="rv rv-d1">{{ hero_heading | safe }}</h1>
    <p class="rv rv-d2">{{ hero_sub }}</p>
    <div class="phero__cta rv rv-d3"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="/projects/">See Our Work <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 8h11M9 4l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg></a><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/contact/">Talk to Us</a></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cols">
      <div class="prose rv">
        <p class="eyebrow">{{ story_eyebrow }}</p>
        <h2 style="font-size:clamp(30px,3.8vw,50px)">{{ story_heading }}</h2>
        {% for para in story_paragraphs %}<p>{{ para }}</p>{% endfor %}
      </div>
      <div class="rv rv-d1">
        <div class="tiles" style="background:var(--line)">
          {% for t in tiles %}<div class="tile"><b>{{ t.value }}</b><span>{{ t.label }}</span></div>{% endfor %}
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top:22px">
      <table class="spec">
        <caption>{{ registered_table.caption }}</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">Specification</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{% for row in registered_table.rows %}<tr><td data-l="Item">{{ row.item }}</td><td data-l="Spec">{{ row.spec }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
      </table></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec stmt">
  <svg class="stmt__wm" viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
    <path d="M13 4V93.5" stroke="#0B0F0D" stroke-width="13"/><path d="M6.5 87H97" stroke="#0B0F0D" stroke-width="13"/>
    <path d="M13 51A36 36 0 0 1 49 87" stroke="#0B0F0D" stroke-width="13"/><circle cx="74" cy="47" r="8" fill="#0B0F0D"/>
  </svg>
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow rv">{{ vision_eyebrow }}</p>
    <blockquote class="rv rv-d1"><p>{{ vision_quote | safe }}</p></blockquote>
    <div class="stmt__body rv rv-d2">
      <p>{{ vision_text }}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec sec--dark">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec__head">
      <div class="sec__label"><p class="eyebrow eyebrow--on-dark">{{ method_eyebrow }}</p><h2 class="rv">{{ method_heading }}</h2></div>
      <p class="rv rv-d1">{{ method_intro }}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      {% for step in method_steps %}
      <div class="step"><span class="step__n">{{ step.number }}</span><h3>{{ step.title }}</h3><p>{{ step.description }}</p><span class="step__bar"><i></i></span></div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec__head">
      <div class="sec__label"><p class="eyebrow">{{ materials_eyebrow }}</p><h2 class="rv">{{ materials_heading }}</h2></div>
      <p class="rv rv-d1">{{ materials_intro }}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cols">
      <div class="rv">
      <table class="spec">
        <caption>{{ turf_table.caption }}</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">Specification</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{% for row in turf_table.rows %}<tr><td data-l="Item">{{ row.item }}</td><td data-l="Spec">{{ row.spec }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
      </table></div>
      <div class="rv rv-d1">
      <table class="spec">
        <caption>{{ indoor_table.caption }}</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">Specification</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{% for row in indoor_table.rows %}<tr><td data-l="Item">{{ row.item }}</td><td data-l="Spec">{{ row.spec }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
      </table></div>
    </div>
    <div class="cols" style="margin-top:34px">
      <div class="rv">
      <table class="spec">
        <caption>{{ drainage_table.caption }}</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">Specification</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{% for row in drainage_table.rows %}<tr><td data-l="Item">{{ row.item }}</td><td data-l="Spec">{{ row.spec }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
      </table></div>
      <div class="prose rv rv-d1">
        <h3>{{ why_publish_heading }}</h3>
        {% for para in why_publish_paragraphs %}<p>{{ para }}</p>{% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec sec--chalk">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec__head">
      <div class="sec__label"><p class="eyebrow">{{ team_eyebrow }}</p><h2 class="rv">{{ team_heading }}</h2></div>
    </div>
    <div class="prose rv rv-d1" style="max-width:760px">
      <p>{{ team_text }}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec sec--dark">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec__head">
      <div class="sec__label"><p class="eyebrow eyebrow--on-dark">{{ why_eyebrow }}</p><h2 class="rv">{{ why_heading }}</h2></div>
      <p class="rv rv-d1">{{ why_intro }}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cards" style="background:#2a2e33">
      {% for c in why_cards %}
      {% set _d = loop.index0 %}
      <article class="card rv{% if _d > 0 %} rv-d{{ _d if _d < 4 else 3 }}{% endif %}" style="background:#0B0F0D">
        <span class="card__n" style="color:#5d646b">{{ c.number }}</span>
        <svg class="card__ico" viewBox="0 0 100 100" style="stroke:#4D8CD4" aria-hidden="true">{% for p in c.icon_path.split('|') %}<path d="{{ p }}"/>{% endfor %}</svg>
        <h3 style="color:#fff">{{ c.title }}</h3>
        <p style="color:#8b939b">{{ c.description }}</p>
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <ul class="list-check" style="margin-top:34px">
      {% for item in why_checklist %}
      {% set parts = item.split(' — ') %}
      <li><strong style="color:#fff">{{ parts[0] }}</strong> — {{ parts[1] }}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cta">
  <div class="wrap cta__row">
    <div><h2 class="rv">{{ cta_heading }}</h2><p class="rv rv-d1">{{ cta_text }}</p></div>
    <div class="cta__btns rv rv-d2">
      <a class="btn btn--dark" href="/contact/">Get a Free Consultation <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 8h11M9 4l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg></a>
      <a class="btn btn--dark" href="https://wa.me/{{ site.whatsapp_number }}?text={{ site.whatsapp_default_message | urlencode }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WhatsApp Us</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
